an employee at Buffalo Wild Wings in  Massachusetts has died after being  exposed to a chemical cleaning agent  hazmat crews were called to the  Burlington restaurant yesterday after  reports of a chemical reaction in the  kitchen fire officials say a male worker  was cleaning the floor with a product  that contains sodium hypochlorite which  is used as a bleaching agent the man was  taken to the hospital where he later  died at least 10 other customers and  workers were hospitalized federal health  officials are investigating the incident
 

